notified when a"] [121 1 "// callable handles it or it is blocked, else ignored or the default."] [148 1 "// killSignal is kill(pid, sig). The own process's signal with a Python handler, not blocked, is delivered here"] [149 1 "// and its handler run before kill returns, as the kernel delivers it to the calling thread before kill returns"] [150 1 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches the handler)."] [162 1 "// the interval timers (ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL, ITIMER_PROF), counted in wall time"] [176 1 "// setItimer arms which's timer (value 0 disarms), returning the old value and interval."] [195 3 "// disarmed: an expiry not yet handled is dropped, as the kernel's single pending bit is taken by the"] [196 3 "// handler that disarms it"] [216 5 "// a Python handler: delivered here, under the timer's lock, so a disarmed timer sends no more"] [217 5 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches it)"] [262 4 "// as at CPython's start: SIGINT's default_int_handler, SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored, the rest SIG_DFL"] [379 5 "// the C handler runs inside raise(): the Python handler before raise_signal returns"] [402 4 "// set_wakeup_fd(fd, /, *, warn_on_full_buffer=True)"] [511 5 "// only the main thread runs handlers: wait for any arrival"] [515 4 "// until a signal is pending (a stale wake-up token is not one)"] [568 7 "// delivered on unblocking: the default action or nothing"] [639 5 "// the own process's signal (a pidfd of another process times out here, harmlessly) handled"] [640 5 "// before the call returns, as the kernel delivers it"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[53 35] [73 26] [99 12] [99 22] [111 60] [141 22] [156 50] [264 14] [264 24] [301 31] [316 14] [316 24] [318 39] [343 40] [365 26] [385 63] [421 37] [438 32] [453 31] [495 37] [544 14] [544 24] [573 40] [604 40] [627 35] [635 104] [642 16] [642 61]]} (go/file "builtins_signal.go" :imports [


